92186045417] [17592186180329 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7c3d2c30-5670-5fd1-b7ab-ba45846770a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180329 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180330 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180330 #edb/ref 1061 145223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180330 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "722361bb-fbdd-5022-9a09-ef207ea9aac6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180330 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180331 #edb/ref 1061 145227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180331 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "418accc5-76da-5990-82d0-b1dc44c3900a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180331 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180786 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we have the following arithmetic sequence with first term $a_1 = {\\color{red}4}$ and common difference  $d={\\color{blue}{3}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{4}},7,10,13,16,\\ldots\n$$\n\nEach term is ${\\color{blue}{3}}$ more than the previous, starting with ${\\color{red}{4}}.$ Therefore, we can express this sequence recursively:\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = a_n + {\\color{blue}{3}}, \\quad a_1 = {\\color{red}{4}}, \\quad n\\geq 1\n$$\n\nWe can also express the sequence using function notation:\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = f(n) + {\\color{blue}{3}}, \\quad f(1) = {\\color{red}{4}}, \\quad n\\geq 1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180786 #edb/ref 1065 8908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180786 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b35c0f06-cff3-51a8-97f6-3a4d39086781" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180786 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
